From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Taylor-Jones <graham.taylor-jones@cargt.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:19:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] imx91-cargt-00363: tuned RGMII pads on the 00365; eMMC
 out of HS400

- imx91-cargt-00363-00365: the dts carried the NXP EVK pad values
  (0x57e data, 0x5fe clocks) for EQOS and FEC. The iMX93 00365 dts uses
  the tuned 0x50e (MDC/MDIO) / 0x51e (RGMII) values for the same
  carrier, so use those on iMX91 too. The kernel dts gets the same
  change.
- imx91-cargt-00363-00365 and -osm-som defconfigs: turn off
  MMC_HS400_SUPPORT and MMC_HS400_ES_SUPPORT, matching the i.MX93 00363
  defconfigs, so U-Boot runs the eMMC at HS200. The SOM DT has one
  usdhc1 pinctrl state for all speed modes. HS400 is disabled in U-Boot
  only, because of U-Boot's support for some eMMC parts. HS400 has
  always worked in Linux, so the kernel dts keeps it.

Backport of meta-imx-cargt wrynose 0881b68 (!56) and the HS400 part of
!45, by Tim Carney.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Cargt board support]
Signed-off-by: Graham Taylor-Jones <graham.taylor-jones@cargt.com>
---
 arch/arm/dts/imx91-cargt-00363-00365.dts    | 56 ++++++++++-----------
 configs/imx91-cargt-00363-00365_defconfig   |  4 +-
 configs/imx91-cargt-00363-osm-som_defconfig |  4 +-
 3 files changed, 32 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

